In article <MIKE.91Jun3133900@apex.yorku.ca> mike@apex.yorku.ca (Mike Marques) writes:
>If you kill the Wizard of Yendor and eat him does he keep on coming
>after you or does that stop him for good? 
There is a difference between reincarnation en reviving. Reincarnation is a
spirit that left a body and takes an other. Reviving is a dead body that
gets a new spirit (not necessarily the same as the previous one). A Troll
revives and if you zap a wand of undead turning on your dead dog it will
also revive, however with a new spirit so it will not recognize you.

The Wizard of Yendor reincarnates, so that answers your question.

